- **User Request**: The user asks the assistant: "I want to file my 2024 taxes correctly. I'm married filing jointly in Chicago IL. W-2 from Desert Sun Logistics: $79,400. Additional income: $8,900 (IT contracting, 3 clients), $920 from Discover Bank savings, $320 from Fidelity. Home office: 100 sq ft exclusive; I pay $2,400/month for 780 sq ft. Deductions: $4,100 student loan interest (MOHELA, 2016–2019); $1,400 to Local United Way have receipt; $890 unreimbursed expenses. Can you tell me what I can deduct, whether to itemize or take the standard deduction, how to treat the home office, and what forms I need?"
